      "judgment_rationale": "Web owns the provider list-backed CRUD controls, assignments, system resilience, model catalog and environment detection exposed by ProviderList and its production component closure. ProviderConfigModal binds listTypes across Web, Cloud Desktop and Local Desktop, while model search filters the fetched catalog client-side; uncalled get-by-id, tenant-provider and server-search service methods are not surface authority. Provider usage requires tenant membership for regular users, while global admins may inspect usage without tenant scoping. Desktop now has a real production loader, App binding and native provider settings surface. Its management Snapshot observations omit the authority_revision required by Snapshot v4, so both modes fail closed to capability_authority_revision_unavailable while retaining the reviewed Cloud and vault-safe Local contracts. Neither Desktop mode claims delete, tenant assignment, system authority or OAuth without a callback contract."
