      "local_deviation": "Tenant webhook registration and secret rotation require an addressable Cloud service authority. Local Desktop keeps the native route contract but does not create an unaudited host callback service.",
      "judgment_rationale": "Webhooks is a registered canonical tenant route backed by the tenant webhook service. Creation requires an event selected from the event type catalog, and that catalog is served by /events/types behind the events feature gate; a disabled or failed catalog is therefore a structured unavailable or error state for creation rather than an ungated tenant-admin action. Webhook CRUD and secret copy remain tenant-admin operations without that feature gate. Desktop has a real production loader, App binding, typed client, controller and native Cloud management page with the reviewed CRUD and event-catalog contracts. The route now binds its stable tenant scope revision around resource reads and preserves the administrator and feature-gate checks for every mutation. Local remains explicitly cloud-only rather than an external-browser fallback."
